  "claims": [
    "Path-valued substitution and higher naturality allow zero/multiple edge images without arbitrary parallel-path generators.",
    "Sequential/tensor exchange for two full proof tracks has exactly their union support.",
    "PathResidual.Contract separates source roots from actual target roots. Residual support may shrink; generated contextual and whole-track comparison support equals original support.",
    "A repaired joint law retains correlated past, shared state and input in one updated checked model.",
    "Actual erased unit-identity wire and MAC roots combine in one source path. The explicit sampled-outcome copy/discard context comparison retains exactly stage and stage+1 guards.",
    "Existing suffix-fusion expansion instantiates the API with two genuine edges; its local expansion is reused, not newly discovered.",
    "Actual sequential/tensor wire-pass fusion residuals use canonical-wire fusion followed by an expanded eighteen-law proof; higher compatibility is not yet provided."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "The fusion residuals in these nine modules lack higher wire-pass compatibility squares.",
    "The contextual PathResidual contract targets Exchange homotopies; its generalization to an arbitrary presented basis remains open, despite a separately available support backend.",
    "Pure-wire higher coherence, full mixed critical-overlap classification, finite complete local basis and complete root coverage remain open.",
    "No fair total-cost advantage over ordinary shared proofs, minimality of guards or time bound is established.",
    "No new computational reduction, native execution integration, key-generation implementation or MAC security bound is derived.",
    "Joint equality holds inside the updated model; it is not arbitrary cross-model equality.",
    "Unregistered NativeConfiguredMAC integration is outside this full build.",
    "Novelty remains unconfirmed; no new external primary-source review in this stage."
  ],
